In case (5) each gauge coupling is irrelevant at the fixed point of the other node. The sum of the two one-loop coefficients is non-negative, so that both cannot be negative, and case (5) does not occur.

In case (3) a coupling that is irrelevant at the free fixed point becomes relevant at the fixed point of the other node. A superpotential is the only way to realize it.

