\section{Anomaly cancellation}

Every chiral multiplet contributes to the cubic anomaly of the gauge group $SU(N)$ through its representation. A multiplet in the fundamental representation and one in the antifundamental representation contribute with opposite signs. A theory with equal numbers of the two is therefore free of the gauge anomaly.

The theories that satisfy this condition are listed in the next Section.

